import java.util.ArrayList;

public class WordFilter {
    /** Removes from words every String whose length is less than minLength.
     *  The order of the remaining Strings is not changed. */
    public static void removeShort(ArrayList<String> words, int minLength) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static void removeShort(ArrayList<String> words, int minLength) {
        for (int i = words.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (words.get(i).length() < minLength) {
                words.remove(i);
            }
        }
    }
```

