public class GridBorder {
    /** Returns the sum of the elements that are in the first row, the last row, the first column
     *  or the last column of grid. Each element is counted once.
     *  Precondition: grid is rectangular with at least one row and one column. */
    public static int borderSum(int[][] grid) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int borderSum(int[][] grid) {
        int sum = 0;
        for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
                if (r == 0 || r == grid.length - 1 || c == 0 || c == grid[r].length - 1) {
                    sum += grid[r][c];
                }
            }
        }
        return sum;
    }
```

